cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Prime Tread Wheel: Counting numbers on a wheel that grows by one tick per layer"
authors:
  - family-names: Gaskin
    given-names: Sylvan
    name-suffix: "\"Obi\""
abstract: >-
  A wheel that grows by one unit per layer (period T(m) = m(m+1)/2) on which
  the counting numbers are rolled; the stagger field of that growth yields
  exact theorems on primality in layers, a certified covering-number bracket
  d(1500) in [42, 45] (both ends solver-free, pure-integer certificates), a
  48-rotation Local Rigidity witness, and an 89-theorem zero-sorry Lean 4 +
  mathlib formalization. See WHITEPAPER.md §14 for the itemized credit
  demarcation against independent prior work (Tucker, Zenodo 2026-09-23).
version: 1.0.2
date-released: 2026-11-17
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24266492"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - prime gaps
  - covering systems
  - Jacobsthal function
  - twin primes
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - exact-integer certificates
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cosmolalia/prime-tread-wheel"
references:
